index 0000000..9547b0c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/BALANCE_MOD.md
@@ -0,0 +1,158 @@
+# Balance Mod
+
+Goal: maximize verified coding result per unit of model spend, token budget,
+wall time, and Android device resources. The mod must prefer deterministic local
+work and DeepSeek Flash, and escalate only when host-observed evidence proves the
+cheaper path is not progressing.
+
+## Non-negotiable development rule
+
+No real provider key is needed during mod development. The first real DeepSeek
+call happens only after the offline prototype and its mock scenarios pass.
+
+## What upstream Reasonix already owns
+
+Do not duplicate these systems:
+
+- `control.Controller`: one orchestration layer behind CLI, HTTP/SSE and desktop.
+- `recovery.Gate`: repeated-operation / episode failure budgets and recovery.
+- `evidence`: progress signatures, delivery evidence, readiness/finalization gates.
+- `checkpoint`: snapshots, rewind and recovery primitives.
+- Context Engine: cache-stable prefix, compaction and bounded tool output.
+- billing: fixed-point money and host-generated `CostQuote`.
+- task budget: post-round cost/time/token ceilings.
+- CodeGraph / project analysis used by the existing agent.
+
+Balance Mod extends these seams rather than implementing parallel copies.
+
+## Mod sections
+
+### 1. APK control and telemetry bridge — v0.1 in progress
+
+Namespace: `/mod/*` on existing `reasonix serve`.
+
+- `GET /mod/status`
+- `GET /mod/budget`
+- `POST /mod/budget`
+- `POST /mod/budget/reset`
+- `GET /mod/resources`
+- `GET /mod/events` (typed SSE, content-free)
+
+The Android UI must consume JSON/SSE state, never parse terminal output.
+
+### 2. KZT Money Governor — v0.1 foundation
+
+APK policy:
+
+- total task/session budget in KZT
+- reserve percentage for final verification/repair
+- maximum Pro share
+- hard-stop toggle
+- explicit FX conversion map (no hard-coded exchange rate)
+
+Accounting reuses `billing.Amount` fixed-point arithmetic. Usage is observed from
+host-generated `CostQuote`; the mod does not reprice provider tokens itself.
+The existing Reasonix task-cost budget is reused as a second post-round stop
+when the active billing currency can be converted from the configured KZT cap.
+
+A strict pre-call admission gate is intentionally not claimed in v0.1; it needs
+to live at provider-call/router admission, where a conservative next-call cost
+can be bounded before network spend occurs.
+
+### 3. Power / model router — next
+
+Target state machine:
+
+`Flash A -> verify -> Flash B (different strategy) -> verify -> Pro diagnosis -> Flash repair`
+
+Pro is a bounded diagnostician, not the default executor. Escalation is based on
+host-observed failures/progress, not on a model requesting a stronger model.
+
+### 4. Anti-loop extension — next
+
+Reuse `recovery.Gate`, evidence progress signatures and existing repeat-failure
+state. Add strategy diversity / state fingerprinting only where upstream does
+not already distinguish genuine progress.
+
+### 5. Verification extension — next
+
+Reuse evidence/readiness/completion receipts. Add deterministic build/test/lint
+policies and APK-visible verifier status. `DONE` remains a host decision backed
+by evidence, never a model assertion.
+
+### 6. Context-cost extensions — next
+
+- compiler/build log root-cause reducer; full logs remain local
+- diff/relevant-line projection
+- impact-test selection using existing graph/project information
+
+### 7. Repair / recovery extensions — next
+
+- dynamic patch governor
+- deterministic-fix whitelist with checkpoint-before-mutation
+- automatic rollback on measurable regression
+- persistent proven-failure cache keyed by environment + error + affected state
+
+### 8. Mobile resource governor — v0.1 telemetry foundation
+
+Linux/PRoot reads only available host facts:
+
+- `/proc/meminfo`
+- `/proc/loadavg`
+- accessible `/sys/class/thermal/*`
+- filesystem free/total space
+
+If Android/PRoot hides thermal sensors, temperature remains absent instead of
+being guessed. Later policy will serialize heavy local builds/tests when memory,
+load, storage or available thermal data says the phone is under pressure.
+
+## APK contract
+
+Example budget request:
+
+```json
+{
+  "budgetKzt": 1000,
+  "reservePercent": 15,
+  "proMaxPercent": 25,
+  "hardStop": true,
+  "fxKztPerUnit": {"USD": 500}
+}
+```
+
+The FX value above is only an example/test fixture. Production must use an
+explicit current rate supplied by the user/UI or a later trusted rate source.
+
+Typed mod events include:
+
+- `budget.configured`
+- `budget.updated`
+- `budget.reserve_entered`
+- `budget.pro_limit_reached`
+- `budget.exhausted`
+- `budget.reset`
+- `resource.snapshot`
+
+Future phases add `loop.detected`, `strategy.changed`, `model.escalated`,
+`verifier.*`, `rollback.*` and `task.done` without changing the APK transport.
+
+## Offline mock provider
+
+The CLI binary registers `kind = "mock"`. It performs no network access and
+needs no API key. A project can temporarily select it for offline validation:
+
+```toml
+default_model = "balance-mock"
+
+[[providers]]
+name = "balance-mock"
+kind = "mock"
+model = "smoke"
+base_url = "http://127.0.0.1"
+context_window = 1000000
+price = { cache_hit = 0, input = 0, output = 0, currency = "KZT" }
+```
+
+`smoke` deterministically asks Reasonix to `read_file`, then `grep`, then emits
+`OFFLINE_MOCK_PASS`. `repeat-failure` repeatedly requests a missing read so the
+existing recovery/anti-loop path can be tested without spending tokens.
